{
  "id": "ep156",
  "duration": 55.502,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.101,
      "text": "A secret radioactive clock is bolted to the side of Voyager.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager spacecraft.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager_spacecraft.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.101,
      "end": 15.995,
      "text": "In 1977, NASA launched twin robotic probes into space, carrying identical gold-plated phonograph records as time capsules for extraterrestrial civilizations.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Mounting-the-golden-record 30269499363 o.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mounting-the-golden-record_30269499363_o.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.1,
          "end": 16.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 15.995,
      "end": 25.816,
      "text": "The recordings hold natural sounds of thunder and whale songs, spoken greetings in 55 languages, and Ann Druyan's brainwaves while falling in love.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Ann Druyan 1.jpg",
        "credit": "Bob Lee",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ann_Druyan_1.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 16.0,
          "end": 25.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 25.816,
      "end": 33.511,
      "text": "Committee chair Carl Sagan even added a pulsar map locating our solar system relative to 14 pulsars.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 25.8,
          "end": 33.5,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 33.511,
      "end": 46.03,
      "text": "To protect the records, engineers fitted an aluminum cover electroplated with an ultra-pure sample of uranium-238, which has a half-life of approximately 4.5 billion years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Uranium238.jpg",
        "credit": "Greenhorn1",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uranium238.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 33.5,
          "end": 46.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 46.03,
      "end": 55.152,
      "text": "By measuring that radioactive decay, any finder can read the record's precise age, deciphering how long ago Earth sent its cosmic message.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager spacecraft.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager_spacecraft.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 46.033,
          "end": 55.5,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
